# Project structure

This document defines the canonical repository layout and the responsibilities of each top-level area.

## Root layout

```text
daemon-core/
├── .github/
├── assets/
├── config/
├── docs/
├── ipc/
├── services/
├── themes/
├── daemon-shared/
├── daemon-theme/
├── daemon-greeter/
├── daemon-lockscreen/
├── daemon-bar/
├── daemon-dashboard/
├── daemon-notifications/
├── daemon-controlcenter/
├── daemon-wallpaper/
├── README.md
├── AGENT.md
├── ARCHITECTURE.md
├── CHANGELOG.md
├── LICENSE
└── .markdownlint.json
```

## Directory responsibilities

### `assets/`

Shared, non-business assets such as fonts, icons, wallpaper samples, and sound resources.

### `config/`

Configuration defaults and schema validation.

### `docs/`

Project documentation and specifications.

### `ipc/`

Adapters for external protocols and system interfaces.

### `services/`

Business logic and system integration services.

### `themes/`

Installed and shipped themes, each with a theme manifest and asset directories.

### `daemon-shared/`

Reusable UI primitives for all modules.

### `daemon-theme/`

Theme engine and validation logic.

### `daemon-greeter/`

Login and authentication UI.

### `daemon-lockscreen/`

Lockscreen UI.

### `daemon-bar/`

Top status bar.

### `daemon-dashboard/`

Launcher and dashboard surfaces.

### `daemon-notifications/`

Notification center and popup logic.

### `daemon-controlcenter/`

Quick settings surface.

### `daemon-wallpaper/`

Wallpaper management and rendering.

## Rules

- One responsibility per directory.
- Feature modules must remain independent.
- No component may create a custom config directory.
- No service may render UI directly.

## Canonical file naming

- lowercase names
- no spaces
- no accidental suffixes in schema files
- stable, descriptive names



